WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.950 --> 00:00:02.649
Welcome to Kinesis.

2
00:00:02.649 --> 00:00:08.685
With your running profile complete, this is where
you plan, record, and understand your training.

3
00:00:09.385 --> 00:00:11.700
Start by adding your running shoes.

4
00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:16.014
Every result you record adds to
the mileage of the pair you wore.

5
00:00:16.714 --> 00:00:20.311
Next, create a cycle with
your goal and a target date.

6
00:00:20.311 --> 00:00:24.892
It can be a race or a personal
goal, like running ten kilometers.

7
00:00:24.892 --> 00:00:28.853
If you like, generate a plan
with the phases of your cycle.

8
00:00:29.553 --> 00:00:34.337
In Request Workouts, set the days,
times, and how long you can train.

9
00:00:34.337 --> 00:00:40.015
Kinesis prepares a weekly proposal, with
the forecast, for you to review and apply.

10
00:00:40.015 --> 00:00:44.643
If you prefer to build your own plan,
you can also import a spreadsheet.

11
00:00:45.343 --> 00:00:47.537
Your workouts live in the calendar.

12
00:00:47.537 --> 00:00:51.576
If your week changes, just drag
the workout to another day.

13
00:00:52.276 --> 00:00:55.797
With a connected watch, you
can send workouts to it.

14
00:00:56.776 --> 00:01:03.629
After your run, import the result from your
watch, upload the FIT file, or enter it manually.

15
00:01:03.629 --> 00:01:07.959
To complete the workout, rate your
perceived effort from one to five.

16
00:01:08.659 --> 00:01:12.132
With the result saved, ask
for a workout analysis.

17
00:01:12.132 --> 00:01:17.846
Your training memory brings your history
together and shows where each detail came from.

18
00:01:18.546 --> 00:01:26.366
Your personal records for five and ten kilometers, the
half marathon, and the marathon update with your results.

19
00:01:27.066 --> 00:01:28.737
You're all set to begin.

20
00:01:28.737 --> 00:01:30.087
Happy running!
